From 3b57370165619de07dff8bfb90a857cb002ef3c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Goehring <dgoehrin@os.amperecomputing.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Jun 2025 18:32:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/36] bkpt: SMP updates wrt future target detach support

This patch provides the framework for future support where CPU targets
in a SMP group can be transitioned back to the non-examined state.

Targets in a SMP group may not all be examined. Before modifying
breakpoint/watchpoint state for a processor core
contained in a SMP group, verify the core has been examined.

For software breakpoints, assign the breakpoint to the current
selected processor target, not the first target in the SMP group.
The first target in the SMP group may be in the non-examined state.

Also verify at least one target in a SMP group is examined
before setting the breakpoint/watchpoint, otherwise
generate an error to the user.

Change-Id: I9923ed20ea02ad92cce5ea12558f95e0ae1b161a
Signed-off-by: Daniel Goehring <dgoehrin@os.amperecomputing.com>
---
 src/target/breakpoints.c | 122 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 82 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/target/breakpoints.c b/src/target/breakpoints.c
index a08041629..fd7f7ac52 100644
--- a/src/target/breakpoints.c
+++ b/src/target/breakpoints.c
